id: elemental-blade
name: Elemental Blade
kind: crafting
types: physical, energy
slots: 2
choices: elementalDark=Elemental (Dark), elementalEarth=Elemental (Earth), elementalFire=Elemental (Fire), elementalIce=Elemental (Ice), elementalLight=Elemental (Light), elementalLightning=Elemental (Lightning), elementalMetal=Elemental (Metal), elementalPlantlife=Elemental (Plantlife), elementalPoison=Elemental (Poison), elementalWater=Elemental (Water), elementalWind=Elemental (Wind)
special: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Special. An Elemental Profile chosen when it is made, added to attacks with it through the
  Multi-Profile Super Profile.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: Upon creating this Weapon, select a Profile with ‘Elemental’ in the name. Apply the
  Multi-Profile Super Profile to any Attacking Maneuvers you use, with the Profile selected for
  the Multi-Profile Super Profile being the Elemental Profile you selected. If it meets the
  Prerequisites, also apply the Compressed Element Disadvantage to those Attacking Maneuvers.
text: >
  Elemental Blade: This Weapon is charged with elemental energy.
  –Weapon Type: Physical/Energy
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 2
  –Effects: Upon creating this Weapon, select a Profile with ‘Elemental’ in the name. Apply the
  Multi-Profile Super Profile to any Attacking Maneuvers you use, with the Profile selected for
  the Multi-Profile Super Profile being the Elemental Profile you selected. If it meets the
  Prerequisites, also apply the Compressed Element Disadvantage to those Attacking Maneuvers.

---

# Built in code (use-maneuver.mjs `elementalBlade`), by the table's rulings: only attacks made with
# this Weapon; the Elemental Profile chosen when it is made, as the Multi-Profile's second Profile
# (even the same one as the attack's); Multi-Profile's KP is paid; where the attack already has a
# Super Profile, the player chooses which; and Compressed Element when an Elemental Profile it names
# is on the attack. With two Profiles that mark Squares, the player picks whose mark; both Profiles'
# Threshold effects apply.
